{"texte":"The world's biggest airliner weighs over 500 tonnes, like 300 cars floating in the sky. No balloon, no rotor, nothing holding it up, and no, it's not the engines. Even some textbooks get this wrong. So what's really keeping it up there? Well, it's the wings. They're curved and tilted just a little, so they push air down. And when you push air down, it pushes you back up. You've felt this before. Hand out the car window, tilt it up, and it lifts, your hand's a tiny wing. Plus, air rushes faster over the top, so pressure drops up there, and that's lift. But lift needs speed, the engines just push forward, and at around 280 kilometers an hour the wings take over. So if both engines stop, the plane doesn't drop, it glides, and in 2001, one glided 120 kilometers and everyone survived.","caracteres":["T","h","e"," ","w","o","r","l","d","'","s"," ","b","i","g","g","e","s","t"," ","a","i","r","l","i","n","e","r"," ","w","e","i","g","h","s"," ","o","v","e","r"," ","5","0","0"," ","t","o","n","n","e","s",","," ","l","i","k","e"," ","3","0","0"," ","c","a","r","s"," ","f","l","o","a","t","i","n","g"," ","i","n"," ","t","h","e"," ","s","k","y","."," ","N","o"," ","b","a","l","l","o","o","n",","," ","n","o"," ","r","o","t","o","r",","," ","n","o","t","h","i","n","g"," ","h","o","l","d","i","n","g"," ","i","t"," ","u","p",","," ","a","n","d"," ","n","o",","," ","i","t","'","s"," ","n","o","t"," ","t","h","e"," ","e","n","g","i","n","e","s","."," ","E","v","e","n"," ","s","o","m","e"," ","t","e","x","t","b","o","o","k","s"," ","g","e","t"," ","t","h","i","s"," ","w","r","o","n","g","."," ","S","o"," ","w","h","a","t","'","s"," ","r","e","a","l","l","y"," ","k","e","e","p","i","n","g"," ","i","t"," ","u","p"," ","t","h","e","r","e","?"," ","W","e","l","l",","," ","i","t","'","s"," ","t","h","e"," ","w","i","n","g","s","."," ","T","h","e","y","'","r","e"," ","c","u","r","v","e","d"," ","a","n","d"," ","t","i","l","t","e","d"," ","j","u","s","t"," ","a"," ","l","i","t","t",